docs {
  Lists the people/lines assigned to a specific Webex Calling device — the "Get Device Members"
  endpoint.

  **Parameters**
  - `deviceId` (path) — the device to inspect. This request overrides the collection-level
    `{{deviceid}}` variable with a request-level `vars:pre-request` block set to the `callingDeviceId`
    (not the plain `webexDeviceId`) of a device — use the `callingDeviceId` value returned from
    "List Devices" here, not the generic device ID.

  **Usage**: This will show you any users that are associated with the lines that exist on the
  given device ID. Note the `lineType` field in the response — it tells you whether a given line is
  that user's primary line or a shared-call-appearance of another user's line on this device.

  Reference: https://developer.webex.com/docs/api/v1/device-call-settings/get-device-members

  ---
  *Documentation written by AI (Claude) as a companion to the WebexOne 2026 API Overview session.*
}
